/**
 * TH Sarabun New, as bytes.
 *
 * Every Thai official letter is typed in TH Sarabun New, so the meeting notice
 * this app generates is too — in anything else it does not read as a letter
 * from the fair. The font is the free national font (SIPA/DIP), which may be
 * used and redistributed without a fee.
 *
 * Two things about this file that look odd and are deliberate.
 *
 * It is base64 inside a .js rather than a .ttf read from disk: a serverless
 * bundle only carries what the code imports, so a readFileSync of a font
 * sitting beside this file works locally and throws ENOENT in production —
 * found on the day somebody needs the notice, which is the worst day.
 *
 * It is subsetted to Latin, Thai and a handful of punctuation with the layout
 * tables KEPT (pyftsubset --layout-features='*' --no-hinting). The layout
 * tables are the whole point: a webfont-converted copy of this font, which is
 * what npm offers, has had its Thai GSUB stripped, and without it every tone
 * mark is drawn in the high position — "ผู้เข้าร่วม" comes out as "ผูเขารวม"
 * with the marks floating a line above. Keeping the tables and dropping the
 * hinting also took it from 830 KB to 62 KB.
 */

